11=====================================================================
11 NETWORK 
11=====================================================================

  11Plaintext ..... port 6667
  11TLS/SSL ....... port 6697   (09recommended - gets you user mode +z)
  11Hostnames ..... cloaked; your real IP is not shown to other users
  11Services ...... ChanServ   /msg ChanServ HELP
  11Accounts ...... /msg NickServ REGISTER <pass>  (see ACCOUNTS)

03=====================================================================
03 CHANNELS 
03=====================================================================

  03#SekurNet ........ main lobby - say hi
  03#help ............ questions about the network or your client
  03#gh-monitoring ... GitHub commit/update feed for our projects

  Want your own channel? See 06[ REGISTERING A CHANNEL ] below.

04=====================================================================
04 RULES 
04=====================================================================

  By connecting you agree to the following. 04No exceptions.

   081. Be civil. No harassment, hate speech, threats or doxxing.
   082. No flooding, spamming, advertising or mass-highlighting.
   083. No botnets, drones, clones or connection proxies for abuse.
      Bots are fine if they behave and a channel op allows them.
   084. No warez, cracks, malware, stolen data or illegal content.
   085. No porn or NSFW content outside channels set up for it.
   086. No nick or channel squatting, and no impersonating staff.
   087. Channel ops run their channels; network staff run the network.
      Take disputes to #help, not to the channel you got kicked from.
   088. Don't ask for oper. If we need you, we'll ask you.

  Breaking the rules gets you a kick, a 04K-line or a 04permanent ban -
  our call, no appeals via PM spam. Incidents may be reported to
  your provider. If you wouldn't let your kids do it at home, don't
  do it here.

11=====================================================================
11 ACCOUNTS: REGISTER A NICK 
11=====================================================================

  Register once, then log in each time you connect:

  1. Register:  11/msg NickServ REGISTER <password>
     or         11/REGISTER <account> <password>
     You are logged in at once; the account is named after your nick.
  2. Log in:    11/msg NickServ IDENTIFY <password>
     other name 11/msg NickServ IDENTIFY <account> <pass>

  09Best way: SASL. Put your account and password in your client's
  SASL PLAIN settings and it logs you in while connecting - no
  IDENTIFY needed. Clients with IRCv3 account registration
  (draft/account-registration) can create the account for you.
  TLS users can log in by certificate instead: 11/CERT ADD

  Pick a strong password and keep it to yourself.

06=====================================================================
06 REGISTERING A CHANNEL 
06=====================================================================

  1. Create it and hold op:   11/JOIN #mychannel
  2. Register it:             11/msg ChanServ REGISTER #mychannel <pass>
  3. Keep it alive (optional) 11/msg ChanServ JOIN #mychannel <pass>
     ChanServ stays inside, so the channel survives everyone leaving.

  Lost op after a reconnect? Get it back with:

     11/msg ChanServ IDENTIFY #mychannel <pass>

  Share ops without sharing the password:
     11/msg ChanServ ACCESS #mychannel ADD *!*@their.host o <pass>

  Pick a strong channel password and keep it to yourself.
  Full command list: 11/msg ChanServ HELP

07=====================================================================
07 SECURITY: SCANNED FOR YOUR PROTECTION 
07=====================================================================

  To keep drones, botnets and open proxies out, every connection is
  checked automatically by our 07Protection bundle:

  1. 11DNS blocklists - your IP is looked up in DNSBLs of known
     open proxies, drones and abusive hosts.
  2. 11Proxy scan - your IP may be scanned: the server opens a few
     connections back to your address on common proxy ports (HTTP,
     SOCKS4, SOCKS5) to test whether it relays traffic. It never
     reads your files or data - it only checks for an open proxy.

  Seeing short connections from us in your firewall log right after
  you connect? That is why - nothing is wrong, no action is needed.

  Listed, or found to be an open proxy? The address is 04banned for a
  while. Close the proxy, then ask in 11#help and we will sort it out.

14=====================================================================
14 PRIVACY 
14=====================================================================

  Server logs are kept for abuse handling only and are never sold
  or shared. Staff never ask for your password - 04don't give it out.

10=====================================================================

  Type 11/MOTD to read this again.        09Be smart. Be chill. Have fun.

